{
  "claimable": true,
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "deobfuscation",
  "description": "Cross-SDK de-obfuscation fixtures (server-side normalizer mirror). view_cases pin deobfuscate()/deobfuscate() view derivation byte-for-byte (method + text, ordered); scan_cases pin runDeobfuscatedScan()/run_deobfuscated_scan() end-to-end (detection + via provenance). Both SDK harnesses (sdk/tests/unit/deobfuscation-conformance.test.ts, sdk-python/tests/test_deobfuscation_conformance.py) must produce identical results; a divergence is a release blocker unless recorded in conformance/known-divergences.md. The transforms mirror the server-side normalizer: input cap 64KiB, one composed canonical view (strip-invisible -> fold-confusables(56) -> strip-HTML-comments -> strip-hidden-HTML -> collapse-whitespace), then percent/hex/base64 decoded views (max 5, depth 1, printable-ratio 0.85, dedupe). Views are detection-only and never feed redaction. decision_cases pin escalateViewOnlyAction/escalate_view_only_action: a view-only hit (via present) has no locatable span in the raw text, so a redact resolution escalates to block on pre-delivery paths (identity when via is null). storage_cases pin redactForStorage/redact_for_storage for STORED copies: span redaction (redactBuiltinPii) when via is null, the whole-text '[REDACTED:obfuscated]' placeholder when via is present. policy_cases pin the composed pipeline decision: runConfiguredPiiScan (deobfuscation enabled) -> resolvePiiPolicy -> escalateViewOnlyAction; final_action 'allow' means no detection (resolution never runs). strip-hidden-HTML removes CSS-hidden (display:none, visibility:hidden) and aria-hidden=\"true\" elements, tag AND content, with no separator, so hidden junk cannot split a phrase past a substring scanner; Both SDKs run the pass. ROT13: a `rot13` view is derived from any input carrying at least eight ASCII letters, which is why nearly every case below carries one. It is applied SPECULATIVELY rather than gated on the text looking encoded, and that is the point - deciding whether a string is rot13 before decoding it would be a heuristic sitting in front of a decision path this SDK sells as deterministic, whereas applying an involution and scanning the result needs no judgement. It is derived LAST and sits outside the decoded-candidate cap (that cap bounds per-token candidate explosion; this is one whole-string transform, bounded by construction), so it never displaces another view and never changes an existing case's `via` attribution. Character substitution (leet) is deliberately NOT decoded - it is the one transform in this family that is not information-preserving, and the reasoning is written out in the deobfuscate module docs in both SDKs.",
